      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Insulin resistance is a fundamental feature of type 2 diabetes and is strongly associated with metabolic disorders which predict increased cardiovascular risk, including hypertension and dyslipidaemia. A new class of insulin-sensitizing agents, the thiazolidinediones, reduce insulin resistance and improve glycaemia both as monotherapy and in combination with sulphonylureas or metformin."},
